# Shofe conventions

This repo is **Spring Boot 3 + React/Vite** (not NestJS/Flutter). Keep that stack unless the user asks to migrate.

## Domain
- inDrive-style negotiation: passenger proposes fare, drivers ACCEPT or COUNTER, passenger selects, fare locks.
- Trip transitions only through server services. Log status changes.
- Night Owl is a dedicated safety module (auto night window, PIN, Guardians, SOS, check-ins, quick-help).
- Payments go through `PaymentProvider` (Pesepay first for Zimbabwe, Stripe stub for global). **Never call payment SDKs from the frontend with secret keys.**

## Money & time
- Prefer integer minor units + ISO currency for new money fields; existing `BigDecimal` fare fields stay until a migration phase.
- Store timestamps in UTC; display in the user's local zone.

## Security
- JWT + role checks on every authenticated endpoint.
- Secrets only via environment variables (`PESEPAY_*`, `JWT_SECRET`, DB). Never log secrets, tokens, OTPs, or full phone numbers.
- Third-party HTTP lives under `com.shofe.integrations.*`.

## Work style
- One feature/phase at a time; add or update tests for pricing, state machine, wallet ledger, and payments.
- Do not invent third-party API fields — if unsure, say so and point to official docs.
- Code and comments in English; user-facing copy can later move to i18n files.
